# .hygiene-denylist: private names the pre-push guard must never let reach the
# public repository. `npm run setup:git` copies this example to
# .hygiene-denylist, which is untracked (listed in .gitignore) and never
# published. Fill in YOUR real entries there, never in this example file.
#
# Format, one entry per line:
#   - lines starting with # are comments, blank lines are ignored;
#   - a plain string matches case-insensitively; one of 5 or more characters
#     also inside compound names ("acmecorp" matches "AcmeCorpClient"), a
#     shorter one only as a whole word ("acme" matches "acme-tools", not
#     "acmeClient");
#   - /regex/flags is a JavaScript regular expression ("g" is added).
# A hit is reported as denylist-line-<n> (the line number in this file), so
# the entry itself is never printed.
#
# The file is looked up in the checkout root, then in the main worktree root.
#
# Harmless examples, commented out so a fresh copy blocks nothing; put your
# own entries below them, without the leading #:
# example-internal-codename
# /example-ticket-\d+/i
